.²2 As the subject of a sentence it agrees in gender and number with the
 predicate without reference to the noun to which it refers; {#etad#} ({#SavalA#})
 {#me Danam#}; but many sometimes remain in the neuter; {#etadeva guruzu#}
 {#vfttiH#} <ls>Ms. 2. 206</ls>.
.²3 It often refers to what

 precedes, especially when it is joined with {#idam#} or any other pronoun;
